From 8f629366111775a38001a2d03a07ff1e71ed601d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:59:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 122/638] [AROS] Preserve zero-on-first-commit page semantics

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-3
AI_STATUS: implementation
ROOT_CAUSE: Run 0122 reached cppgc GCInfoTable initialization and failed DCHECK(!base[i]); the pre-MMU Exec fallback removed MEMF_CLEAR for inaccessible reservations, while cppgc makes slices accessible with SetPermissions rather than Recommit, exposing stale physical bytes.
FIX_REASON: Keep MEMF_CLEAR on Exec-backed reservations so every future first-access slice begins zeroed, while permission-only transitions do not erase already committed data.
SCOPE: base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator_internals_aros.h
VALIDATION: PartitionAlloc page_allocator.o cross-compiled; debug.resource artifact 25 identifies gc-info-table.cc:122 after both large pools allocate through the Exec fallback.
RISK: The pre-MMU bridge eagerly clears full physical backing, including the two bounded 1 GiB address pools; this trades startup bandwidth for the anonymous-page zero guarantee until sparse MMU-backed reservation exists.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: tracked Exec reservations -> cppgc first commit through SetPermissions -> stale bytes -> preserve clear backing
Continues: 3e42c47a8e; 19a864b7c2
---
 .../page_allocator_internals_aros.h                | 14 ++++----------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator_internals_aros.h b/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator_internals_aros.h
index 443b244f78..fa1abc8cc4 100644
--- a/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator_internals_aros.h
+++ b/base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/page_allocator_internals_aros.h
@@ -259,16 +259,10 @@ uintptr_t SystemAllocPagesInternal(
       return 0;
     }
 
-    ULONG exec_flags = flags;
-    if (accessibility.permissions ==
-            PageAccessibilityConfiguration::kInaccessible ||
-        accessibility.permissions ==
-            PageAccessibilityConfiguration::kInaccessibleWillJitLater) {
-      exec_flags &= ~MEMF_CLEAR;
-    }
-
-    allocation_base =
-        AllocateExecPages(length, exec_flags, &allocation_length);
+    // This bridge has physical backing even for inaccessible reservations.
+    // Keep it zeroed so the first accessible slice has anonymous-page commit
+    // semantics without destroying data on later permission-only changes.
+    allocation_base = AllocateExecPages(length, flags, &allocation_length);
     if (!allocation_base) {
       s_allocPageErrorCode = ENOMEM;
       if (log_request) {
